# CampusConnect – Logical Vulnerability Fixes

## Overview
After thorough code review, the following logical vulnerabilities have been identified from a **user's POV**. Each issue is categorized with the affected file(s) and the root cause.

---

## Bug Inventory

| # | Severity | Area | Problem |
|---|----------|------|---------|
| 1 | 🔴 High | Backend – Club Controller | **Club admin can join/leave their own club** – no guard prevents the admin from sending a join or leave request, causing data inconsistency |
| 2 | 🔴 High | Backend – Event Controller | **RSVP allowed on past/cancelled events** – `rsvpEvent` does not validate `event.status` or whether the event date has passed |
| 3 | 🔴 High | Backend – Club Controller / Route | **`authorize("clubAdmin","orgAdmin")` on approve/reject does NOT verify the user is the admin of *this specific club*** – any `clubAdmin` role user can approve members on clubs they don't own |
| 4 | 🔴 High | Backend – Auth Controller | **`refreshToken` does not verify the user exists in DB** – a deleted user can keep refreshing tokens indefinitely |
| 5 | 🟡 Medium | Frontend – ClubDetail | **Club admin sees "Request to Join" button** – `!myStatus && user` is true for the admin because the admin is not in the `members` array |
| 6 | 🟡 Medium | Frontend – EventDetail | **Volunteer button shows even when already registered & event is full** – volunteers should not bypass capacity |
| 7 | 🟡 Medium | Frontend – CreateEvent | **Club selector shows ALL clubs fallback when user has no admin clubs** – regular members can see the form but with clubs they don't own |
| 8 | 🟡 Medium | Backend – Club Controller | **`leaveClub` allows the club admin to leave their own club** – club would become admin-less |
| 9 | 🟡 Medium | Backend – Event Model | **Date validator (`v > new Date()`) runs on update too** – editing an already-past event (e.g., to mark as "completed") fails because the saved date is in the past |
| 10 | 🟢 Low | Frontend – AppLayout / Routes | **Admin routes (`/admin`, `/admin/verify`, `/admin/stats`) have NO route-level guard** – only page-level check, allowing brief flash of restricted content |

